<!--T:2-->
You can embed images from [[commons:Main Page|Wikimedia Commons]]. Referenced files are downloaded at build time and stored in the [[<tvar name="2">Special:MyLanguage/Configuration#WikvenAssetDirectory</tvar>|asset directory]] with the rest of what the build generates, so the static site does not depend on Commons when viewed. See [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/InstantCommons</tvar> InstantCommons] for details.

<!--T:3-->
== Local images ==

<!--T:4-->
[[File:<tvar name="1">Bakery oven.jpg</tvar>|thumb|A bakery oven (circa 1850-1900), embedded here as a local image.]]

<!--T:5-->
You can also use your own image files. Put them in your source directory, next to the <code>.wikitext</code> files, and embed them with the [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Help:Images</tvar> usual file syntax]:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
[[File:My photo.png|thumb|A caption]]
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:6-->
PNG, GIF, JPEG, WebP, and SVG files are supported. Raster images are thumbnailed at build time; an SVG is rasterized to a thumbnail when a converter is available, otherwise served inline.

<!--T:7-->
The thumbnailing backend is detected from the tools present at build time: [<tvar name="2">https://imagemagick.org/</tvar> ImageMagick] for raster images when it is installed (as in the Docker image), otherwise the built-in [<tvar name="3">https://libgd.github.io/</tvar> GD] library (as in the standalone [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Standalone binary</tvar>|binary]], which carries GD); SVG uses [<tvar name="4">https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/librsvg</tvar> librsvg] when present, otherwise native inline rendering. The pages render the same either way, ImageMagick simply produces higher-quality thumbnails and supports more formats.

<!--T:8-->
To give a file its own description page, add a wikitext file named after it in the <code>File:</code> namespace, the same way other namespaced pages are named. For <code>My photo.png</code>, that is <code>File:My photo.png.wikitext</code>.
</translate>

